	(text "LRA-12 - what changed, and the one thing to read first"
		(at 845.82 30.48 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.2 2.2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "0cdd2642-7c33-4a37-9380-76b810b00903")
	)
	(text "This is the LRA-06 capture with its eight electrical placeholders\nresolved. Every populated part now carries a checked footprint and\nno dashed NOT SELECTED body remains. The decisions, their\ncalculations and the residual gates are in power/LAYOUT_CLOSURE.md\nand LRA12_HANDOFF.md; read those before changing anything here.\nX1  B2 series isolation      -> ASSR-601JV + 2-FET enable\nX2-X5 other four branches    -> justified bypass, see below\nX6  qualified IGN / QREPORT  -> captured from CUTOFF_MARGIN_REVIEW S2\nX7  vehicle entry protection -> 1.5KE20A + second-stage A5 clamp\nX8  independent cutoff       -> captured from MAX_ON_CUTOFF\nJ1/J2 connectors             -> Molex Mini-Fit Jr., family in service\nQ2/R06-REV-2 opto LED return -> moved from B16 to PGND\nQ4 onboard FIGN              -> dropped; fuse belongs at the tap\nQ5 J4 service UART           -> dropped; J4 is the reset pair only\nQ6 where MAX_ON cuts HOLD    -> QS between SINK and the QH collector"
		(at 845.82 35.56 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "8f04f190-f1b3-48ce-9fa0-2d2a046a12fd")
	)
	(text "The voltage envelope, which is one chain and not five choices"
		(at 845.82 77.66 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.2 2.2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "37f9d057-cabd-4b3f-ae6a-f104221e7533")
	)
	(text "The selected QP is the only P-channel switch the record found with a\nHOT zero-gate leakage maximum (70 uA at 125 C) that fits the 200 uA\nparked allocation; the IRF4905 screen is 250 uA and cannot. That part\nis rated -40 V VDS, so the entry clamp has to hold below 40 V, which\nrules out the inherited 1.5KE30A at 41.4 V - the same 41.4 V that\nalready exceeded QI/QH VCEO and the LM2678 operating ceiling. The\n1.5KE20A clamps at 27.7 V, 29.19 V at 85 C using its own 0.090 %/K\ncoefficient, leaving 10.8 V to every 40 V part.\n29.19 V is still above the contract 28 V protected-rail target, so\nthe A5 regulator gets its own second stage: R_AON 330R and a BZX55C22\nhold P_AON at or below 25.4 V at 85 C, 4.6 V inside the TPS709 30 V\nrecommended maximum. The <=28 V criterion is therefore measured at\nTP_PAON, not at P12.\nSUSTAINED P12 must stay at or below 17.1 V, the clamp standoff. No\nsingle clamp can both stand off a 24 V jump start and limit to 28 V,\nso that exposure is declared excluded rather than quietly assumed\nsurvivable. See LAYOUT_CLOSURE S3 for the two alternatives and\nwhat each would cost."
		(at 845.82 82.74 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "65fee6e9-a530-4aa4-a101-7880fc1d9bae")
	)
	(text "Vehicle inputs: one switch, four justified bypasses"
		(at 845.82 132.46 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.2 2.2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "040903ae-c70f-422a-865d-5f4cb84c6103")
	)
	(text "Five fitted cells, carried forward with no value changed (AS_BUILT S2).\nB2 is the only branch energized with the key out - 4.669 V open\ncircuit, 4.140 V loaded, drawing 140.8 uA of which 109.2 uA was being\nback-fed into the unpowered 3V3 rail through a forward-biased clamp.\nIt gets the series switch, upstream of the divider top as required.\nB1, C14, C11 and B11 are all ignition-fed and measured or logged dead\nwith the key out, so they meet the parked criterion with no device and\nno device leakage. Reaching the board-off-and-energized criterion\nneeds the key on AND an upstream power fault, because ignition\npresent turns QI on and powers the board; in that fault state the\nfitted 7.5k-22k series resistance bounds each branch below 0.7 mA.\nFour more relays would cost 41 mA of awake LED current and four\n10.4 x 7.5 mm packages against a fault-only benefit. Full reachable-\nstate table in LAYOUT_CLOSURE S4.\nBecause no series element enters the fuel or supply top leg, the\ncard header calibration (log.adc.fuel div=7500/4700) still has every\nterm it needs and REV_A_INTERFACES S8.2 needs no change.\nDigital divider bottoms return to PGND. Both ADC divider bottoms,\ntheir filter and clamp returns, J2.6 (B16) and Pico AGND are ONE\nnode. AGND and PGND are already joined INSIDE the Pico module, so\nthat junction is the single point: layout must NOT add a second\nboard-level bond between them."
		(at 845.82 137.54 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "b18c7d13-1b48-4ca1-bfbd-a533783d1979")
	)
	(text "The opto LED return - R06-REV-2 decided"
		(at 845.82 197.42 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.2 2.2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "fe12f707-9d86-49ac-8b89-f4fae1d79a71")
	)
	(text "The fitted cell returned the ignition LED cathode to the B16 cluster\nconductor with nothing in series, putting 4.7-5.8 mA of signal-\ndependent current through the node both ADC channels reference, which\nREV_A_INTERFACES S4 says must never become a power return. D5 and\nthat return cannot both stand. LRA-12 moves the cathode to PGND, the\narrangement DESIGN.md S3 already specified.\nWhat B16 still carries is the two divider return currents, at most\nabout 0.65 mA combined and only while the cluster is energized; those\nare intrinsic to a ratio measurement referenced to cluster ground.\nThe LED current was not.\nConsequence recorded rather than hidden: the LED now returns into the\nboard instead of off-board. It cannot reach any switched rail - the\nopto output side is in the A5 domain and galvanically separate from\nthe LED - so this removes an injection path rather than moving one.\nCTR margin at the measured 2.2k: 3.39 mA of LED current at the 9 V\ncharacterization point against 96 uA of emitter load, 15x on the\n>=50 % CTR at 5 mA. Hot CTR and the 4.5 V ON endpoint stay open."
		(at 845.82 202.50 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "4a7a844c-585c-4f8b-abd3-bb47b5104f71")
	)
	(text "Pico W pin map"
		(at 845.82 249.68 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.2 2.2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "664eba55-669a-404a-967a-629bae54ce52")
	)
	(text "GP0/GP1, GP14/GP15, GP20-GP22 and GP28 are deliberately unconnected.\nGP7 is now ISO_EN, the B2 isolation enable, confirmed free in S1.\nGP8/GP9 (UART1) and GP10 (tied DE//RE) go to the DNP expansion\nheader, with GP13 offered there as a spare - offers, not reservations.\nARM, EXPIRED, PGOOD and HOLD_N stay off the GPIOs: A5-domain test\npoints only, and firmware has no ARM feedback in this revision.\nGP11 and GP12 are brought to pads per S1. ADC_VREF, 3V3_EN and VBUS\nare unconnected as fitted; VBUS has no buck connection.\nNo GPIO carries a pullup to any rail but switched 3V3."
		(at 845.82 254.76 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "ef00ae3b-c0d5-4f8c-bf05-0da3998d6220")
	)
	(text "HOLD driver and the cutoff path"
		(at 845.82 281.62 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.2 2.2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "8d58ac5b-34ce-40f9-9239-6db1b430b63c")
	)
	(text "GP6 HOLD_RAW with a 47k external pulldown and the JH MAINTENANCE\nlink. Firmware latches it LOW before output enable; 4 mA drive,\n2.6 V loaded qualification target.\nQS is the series interruption the independent timer uses: drain to\nSINK, source to the QH collector, body diode blocking the sink\ndirection when off. QI remains wired straight to SINK, so raw\nignition still overrides everything. QMON senses HOLD_RAW ahead of\nJH, so opening JH releases QH without blinding the monitor.\nJH, R_EXPP/R_EXPT and the accelerated 64 s tap are three different\nthings and are labelled as such: JH is maintenance, R_EXPP is the\nproduction 2048 s selection, R_EXPT is the bench test selection and\nis DNP. Fit exactly one of R_EXPP and R_EXPT: they are two counter\noutputs and must never be shorted together."
		(at 845.82 286.70 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "ecfd010c-3f73-4fd3-a928-9b4e1012cd07")
	)
	(text "SD and expansion"
		(at 845.82 323.72 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.2 2.2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "b861fded-9d08-45ee-b2eb-9b4e799dfd27")
	)
	(text "SPI0 at 12 MHz on switched 3V3 only (GP16 MISO, GP17 CS, GP18 SCK,\nGP19 MOSI). D6 bulk is now a selected 47 uF: a 200 mA write spike for\n1 ms inside 100 mV of droop needs 2 uF, so this is an order of\nmargin without an oversized can. Any move of this module to a 5 V\nrail re-opens the MISO clearance gate of AS_BUILT S3.5.\nJ3 is a passive expansion header for a DNP daughterboard. There is\nno transceiver, bias or termination on this board, which is why no\noff-state current claim is needed. A daughterboard may take power\nonly from J3.1 (B5) or J3.3 (switched 3V3), both switched; an\nexternally powered adapter on this header breaks the off-state\ncontract. No bus interoperability is claimed.\nJ4 is the RUN-to-GND reset pair and nothing else."
		(at 845.82 328.80 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "906fb0bc-c970-4dbb-8b23-db90d3bd5218")
	)
	(text "Onboard switched power"
		(at 845.82 363.28 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.2 2.2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e97f2421-7a88-4f29-96ee-74e3b7aae4f6")
	)
	(text "Reuses the existing power candidate as DESIGN.md S3 lists it\n(D-POWER-02), with the reviewed deltas D7 and D13 and the LRA-02\ncomponent selections. The LM2678, its TVS role, bulk capacitors,\nboost cap, inductor value and both Schottky positions all have\nin-service precedent on the keyless board in this car (D-POWER-03);\nthe logger adds QP, QI/QH, DZ, DOR, the A5 rail and MAX_ON.\nRail nets: P12 always-on, P_AON the clamped A5 feed, A5 always-on 5 V,\nVCLK the filtered oscillator rail, VIN_SW switched, B5 buck output,\nVSYS through DOR, P3V3_SW from the Pico regulator.\nRGS is 10k, not the 100k of DESIGN.md S3: the MAX_ON revision needs\nit so that the 0.2 V off-gate limit allows 19.80 uA of total sink\nleakage instead of 2 uA.\nQP body diode is drain-to-source: it blocks P12 to VIN_SW when off\nbut does not block reverse energy, so USB backfeed testing has to\ncover VIN_SW as well as B5. The DPAK tab is DRAIN and carries\nswitched battery voltage - a clearance and thermal item for layout.\nFor every diode, check the NET rather than the footprint name."
		(at 845.82 368.36 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e50d13b5-ab29-435c-aff8-88d23fd51edb")
	)
	(text "Independent cutoff - what it does and does not cover"
		(at 845.82 415.54 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.2 2.2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "bc4e46ec-61a8-475b-b9cf-7b3a4a7834f7")
	)
	(text "Nominal 2048 s from qualified ignition loss, on its own always-on\nsupply and its own clock. The Pico cannot refresh it with HOLD,\nresets, network traffic or watchdog servicing; releasing HOLD disarms\nit, and only a qualified ignition assertion can grant it again.\nReset dominates set in the settled Boolean model. UCOUNT is reset by\nBAD OR IGN_Q and deliberately NOT by NARM, which would erase EXPIRED\nas it disarmed the latch; instead the clock stops when disarmed.\nNot covered, and stated here so nobody reads more into it: a stopped\nclock, failed timer logic, a shorted QS or QP, an ignition line stuck\nhigh, repeated raw pulses that energize QI, or external backfeed. A5\nfaults can remove power before the deadline. No SD integrity claim\nsurvives a forced cutoff.\nEvery unused CMOS input is tied to a rail (ULATCH 12 and 13 to\nground) and every package has its own 100 nF across its own supply\npins - both are layout requirements as much as BOM lines."
		(at 845.82 420.62 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "918d90dc-0b12-4a53-884c-4df15ad86010")
	)
	(text "Test points and ground loops"
		(at 845.82 462.72 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.2 2.2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d451fd0f-e584-4edc-becc-af19847be0f2")
	)
	(text "Twenty-five test loops. Three separate ground loops follow the\nkeyless pattern: buck, Pico and harness end, the last on the bonded\nB16/AGND sense node. J4 shorts RUN to GND for a reset without\ncutting power.\nTP_PAON is where the <=28 V protected-rail criterion is measured.\nTP_GATE against TP_P12 is where the QP -14 to +1 V gate acceptance\nband is measured. TP_CLK32 carries the clock frequency and startup\nmeasurements the whole 2048 s arithmetic rests on.\nCurrent-sensitive nodes must be measurable without the instrument\nsupplying the current being measured, and probes must be removable\nfor the final leakage reading - a layout requirement, not only a\nprocedure."
		(at 845.82 467.80 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "35bd8ae5-7c97-4518-902c-25e0bc68abc9")
	)
	(text "What is still open - none of it a layout blocker"
		(at 845.82 502.28 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.2 2.2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "2a260323-3e95-4056-8782-8f74537f5a52")
	)
	(text "Classified in full in LRA12_HANDOFF.md. In short:\nORDER GATE   ASSR-601JV availability (fallback AQY221N2S specified,\n             strictly smaller, same keepout); exact fuse family and\n             curve; capacitor approval-sheet bias/aging/IR data.\nBRING-UP     A5 ground current below 100 uA load; hot leakage of QP,\n             QI, QH, QMON, QS, QREPORT and the opto; clock startup\n             and loaded ramps; opto ON/OFF endpoints; ASSR turn-on\n             against a 55k rather than the specified 20k test load;\n             assembled rail decay with the larger COUT; LM2678 loop\n             stability with the selected output capacitor.\nVEHICLE      sustained-overvoltage and jump-start exposure; load\n             dump; harness impedance and fuse clearing; long-duration\n             hot and cold operation.\nFIRMWARE     ISO_EN sequencing contract - assert and wait 20 ms before\n             trusting VSS edges, deassert and wait 5 ms before\n             releasing HOLD; GP5 now means hardware-qualified\n             ignition; the 1770/1800/1801 s policy is unchanged.\nNothing here is frozen, ordered or fabricated. A complete, routable\ndesign is not an approved board."
		(at 845.82 507.36 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "8d48a134-f6a6-48b4-b8e4-5a43c6623b1b")
	)
	(sheet_instances
		(path "/"
			(page "1")
		)
	)
	(embedded_fonts no)
)
